invariant: INV-49
file: src/aead_avx2.c
catches: test/lint-frame-align.sh
reason: pass_hashing loses the attribute that makes clang align its frame
  to 32 bytes. Its rounds and its Poly1305 groups store and reload 256-bit
  values in stack slots, and clang then places those slots wherever the
  caller's stack pointer leaves them, so some lie across a cache line or a
  page boundary, as chacha20_avx2.c's pass did before decision 124. Every
  test still passes, because the bytes are the same. gcc aligns the frame
  on its own and CI compiles with gcc, so the lint reads what the pinned
  clang compiles for x86-64.

--- old
__attribute__((force_align_arg_pointer)) static void
pass_hashing(
--- new
static void
pass_hashing(
